From: Duy Truong <duytruong@google.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 05:45:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix integer underflow and OOB access in libnfc-nci

A compromised NFC controller sending repeated unsolicited NFCEE_DISCOVER_NTF messages can trigger an integer underflow in the `nfa_ee_cb.cur_ee` counter. This underflowed value is subsequently used as a loop bound without proper checks, leading to out-of-bounds reads and writes in the ECB array.

This commit resolves the vulnerability by:
1. Introducing an `incremented` boolean flag in `nfa_ee_nci_disc_ntf` to track whether `cur_ee` was advanced. The decrement operation at the end of the function is now gated by this flag, preventing the integer underflow.
2. Adding explicit bounds checking (`xx < NFA_EE_NUM_ECBS`) to multiple loops iterating over `cur_ee` in `nfa_ee_act.cc` and `nfa_ee_main.cc` to strictly safeguard against out-of-bounds pointer traversal.

Test: m libnfc-nci && atest libnfc-nci-tests

Bug: 522366268
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
